---
/**
 * /guide/danger/ — which rooms are dangerous, and why.
 *
 * Gap from content/keywords-game.json. Derived, not invented: every room observation
 * below comes from ROOM_INFO blurbs, which were themselves written from our own
 * in-game screenshots. The intro says that plainly and invites corrections, because
 * "which room is dangerous" is partly a judgement call and the owner knows the map
 * better than the descriptions do.
 *
 * The mechanics side (what makes ANY room dangerous) is all game.ts.
 */
import GuideLayout from '../../layouts/GuideLayout.astro';
import { ROOM_INFO } from '../../data/rooms';
import { JINGLES, WORM, CRUSHERS, EXTRACTION, SCRAPPER, POD } from '../../data/game';

/**
 * Read off our own screenshots via the room blurbs. Light and sightline notes are
 * observations, not config values, so they are kept in one place and labelled.
 */
const RISK: Record<string, { light: string; sightlines: string; hiding: string }> = {
  'central-room': { light: 'Red-lit, glowing globe', sightlines: 'Open hub, walkways off it', hiding: 'Low — it is the crossroads' },
  'cargo-dock': { light: 'Red warning light', sightlines: 'The biggest open space in the bunker', hiding: 'Low — catwalks and crates, but you are seen crossing' },
  'storage-bay': { light: 'Dim aisles', sightlines: 'Long aisles, corners you cannot see past', hiding: 'Good for breaking a sightline, risky if cornered' },
  'control-room': { light: 'One of the brightest rooms', sightlines: 'Banks of consoles, blue screens', hiding: 'Poor — brightness works against you' },
  'nuclear-reactor': { light: 'Very little light', sightlines: 'Red coils and green tanks, tight', hiding: 'Best cover, worst navigation' },
  medbay: { light: 'Blue curtains, cold', sightlines: 'A long centre aisle', hiding: 'Poor — nowhere to hide on the aisle' },
  security: { light: 'Cold blue', sightlines: 'Corridor in, desks and monitors', hiding: 'Mixed — the corridor is the problem' },
  'interrogation-room': { light: 'Harsh, with a red observation window', sightlines: 'Open room, watched through glass', hiding: 'Poor — harsh light and sightlines' },
};

const dangerLd = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Article',
  headline: 'Which rooms in STATIC are dangerous',
  about: { '@id': 'https://beaniestudio.site/#game' },
};
---

<GuideLayout
  title="STATIC Map Danger — Which Rooms to Avoid"
  description={`Which rooms in STATIC are dangerous: light, sightlines and cover for every room, plus what draws the Worm and where Jingles has the advantage.`}
  path="/guide/danger/"
  h1="Which rooms are dangerous"
  kicker="Official guide · Map tactics"
  crumb="Room danger"
  updated="2026-10-14"
  jsonLd={[dangerLd]}
>
  <p class="text-lg">
    No room in STATIC is safe, but they are not equally dangerous. Bright rooms and long aisles favour{' '}
    {JINGLES.name}; dark, cluttered rooms favour you. This page rates every room on light, sightlines
    and cover.
  </p>
  <p class="text-facility-300">
    These notes are read off our own in-game screenshots. They are observations rather than game
    config, so if you know the map better than the descriptions do, tell us in the{' '}
    <a href="/guide/map/">map guide</a> discussion.
  </p>

  <h2 id="table">Room by room</h2>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th scope="col">Room</th>
          <th scope="col">Light</th>
          <th scope="col">Sightlines</th>
          <th scope="col">Cover</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {ROOM_INFO.map((r) => {
          const risk = RISK[r.slug];
          if (!risk) return null;
          return (
            <tr>
              <td class="text-facility-100"><a href={`/guide/map/#${r.slug}`}>{r.name}</a></td>
              <td>{risk.light}</td>
              <td>{risk.sightlines}</td>
              <td>{risk.hiding}</td>
            </tr>
          );
        })}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="winners">Where Jingles has the advantage</h2>
  <p>
    {JINGLES.name} is faster than you ({JINGLES.bloodlust.speedMult}× during Bloodlust, and a dash at{' '}
    {JINGLES.dash.speed} studs per second for {JINGLES.dash.durationSec} seconds). So the Hunter wins
    in any space where the two of you can see each other for long enough to close the gap:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Long, bright aisles.</strong> The Medbay centre aisle is the clearest example — no cover and nowhere to break line of sight.</li>
    <li><strong>Big open rooms.</strong> The Cargo Dock is the largest space in the bunker; crossing it is the risk, not being in it.</li>
    <li><strong>The Control Room.</strong> One of the brightest rooms, which removes your main advantage.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Read the counterplay in <a href="/guide/jingles/">the Jingles guide</a> — the{' '}
    {JINGLES.attack.windupSec}-second wind-up is the window you get to dodge.
  </p>

  <h2 id="yours">Where you have the advantage</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The Nuclear Reactor.</strong> Very little light to see by. Bad for navigating, good for
      not being seen — and <a href="/guide/hiding/">lockers</a> matter less when the room is already dark.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The Storage Bay.</strong> Long aisles of shelving with corners you cannot see past. That
      cuts both ways, but it is the best room for breaking a chase.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anywhere with a teammate.</strong> A {SCRAPPER.reviveHoldSec}-second revive or a{' '}
      {POD.rescueHoldSec}-second pod rescue changes the maths more than any piece of cover.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="anywhere">What makes any room dangerous</h2>
  <p>
    The room matters less than what you are doing in it. Three things turn a safe room into a death
    trap regardless of where it is on the map:
  </p>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto">
    <table class="data-table">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Trigger</th><th scope="col" class="num">Numbers</th><th scope="col">Why it is dangerous</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Ringing the bell</td>
          <td class="num">Worm in {WORM.bellSpawnDelaySec} s, {WORM.bellSpawnDistStuds} studs away</td>
          <td>Always summons one, wherever you are</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Heavy scrap in hand</td>
          <td class="num">&minus;{SCRAPPER.heavyCarrySlowMaxPct}% speed, no flashlight</td>
          <td>Slow, blind, and it attracts Worms</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Noise</td>
          <td class="num">{WORM.baseChancePct}% base, checked every {WORM.baseChanceEverySec} s</td>
          <td>Missed throws and screaming mimics multiply it</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Being the last one up</td>
          <td class="num">pod timer at double speed</td>
          <td>No rescue is coming; the {POD.timerSec} s clock halves</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="plan">A route that works</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Start from the Central Room</strong> and pick a crusher. You need {CRUSHERS.totalKg} kg across {CRUSHERS.count}.</li>
    <li><strong>Search dark rooms first</strong> — the Reactor and the Storage Bay — while the round is quiet.</li>
    <li><strong>Cross the bright rooms deliberately.</strong> The Control Room and Medbay are where you are most visible, so do not linger.</li>
    <li><strong>Finish near the exit.</strong> The {EXTRACTION.room} window is {EXTRACTION.windowSec} seconds and it is per player, so being on the far side of the map when it opens costs you the round.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>
    The extraction flow is in <a href="/guide/crushers/">crushers and minigames</a>, and every room is
    photographed in the <a href="/guide/map/">map guide</a>.
  </p>
</GuideLayout>
